<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: Irish govt to view Tesco deal in due course.</title>
<headline>Irish govt to view Tesco deal in due course.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1997-03-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ireland's Enterprise and Employment minister will examine Friday's announcement by Britain's supermarket chain Tesco Plc that it wants to buy Associated British Foods Plc's Irish food retail business when it is formally notifed, a spokeswoman said. She told Reuters that Minister Richard Bruton &quot;will consider the situation if and when he is formally notified.&quot;</p>
<p>Irish suppliers have voiced concern that they will lose key outlets if ABF's Qunnsworth and Crazy Prices stores are taken over by British interests.</p>
<p>Bruton is currenly on an official visit to the United States and is not expected back in Dublin until Saturday.</p>
<p>-- Dublin Newsroom +353 1 676 9779</p>
</text>
